usage: frontier_sweep.py [-h]
                         {stats,sweep,greedy,exactness,cross-check,analyze}
                         ...

M1 frontier sweep: exact group omission on real Qwen3 checkpoints.
Subcommands, each of which writes its own receipt: stats calibration group
statistics and selector rankings exactness instrument gates G1 on real held-
out windows, plus the files for the independent Rust cross-check cross-check
compare the Python and Rust masked partial sums sweep evaluate arms on the
held-out split (uniform | layers | greedy | control) analyze bootstrap CIs,
the frontier JSON, the SVG plot and the table The contract is
`docs/EXPERIMENT-CONTRACT.md`, registered before any of this ran. Nothing here
trains, samples text or reads held-out text for selection. All arithmetic is
f32 with TF32 disabled; the teacher is the dense f32 model.

positional arguments:
  {stats,sweep,greedy,exactness,cross-check,analyze}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
